 "skeptic": {
  "verdict": "weakened",
  "objection": "The seller is the open question, and the first pass never tested it. The county roll sends the owner's tax bills to 650 West Peachtree St NW, which Norfolk Southern's own site gives as its Real Estate Department. The parcel adjoins a 25.5-acre tract owned by Central of Georgia Railroad Co, about 400 ft from the NS line, so this looks like railroad land next to railroad land, held since 2007. NS names two real-estate channels: sales to non-shipping customers, and strategic sales for its core business and freight customers. Its site does not say which channel this tract belongs to, whether it is held for rail-served or operating use, or whether the 'ET AL' co-owners would sell to a non-rail warehouse buyer. The market verdict no_sign_found rests only on empty rezoning and special-use queries, which say nothing about the owner's intent. Second doubt: the by_right zoning verdict rests on the 1982 ordinance, while ATL Zoning 2.0 brings a new official zoning map that renames every district. Its adoption and the new name for this I-1 lot were not confirmed. Nothing found kills the lead. Zoning and location checks hold up: the map point is in this parcel, and every lot within 60 ft of its outline is I-1 or I-1-C, with no residential lot.",
